+    With ``pool_size > 1``, every layer that performs XQA decode is assigned a
+    stable slot. Slot 0 reuses the legacy global workspace buffer
+    (``_get_trtllm_workspace_buffer()``); slots 1..N-1 are independent CUDA
+    workspaces allocated lazily (``torch.zeros`` of
+    ``envs.VLLM_FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BUFFER_SIZE`` bytes), so a pool of size 2
+    adds exactly one extra buffer. The first 8MiB of each workspace is used by
+    FlashInfer XQA as semaphores, so independent buffers let the diagnostic
+    observe per-layer interference.
