+    Slot assignment is memoized on the layer's ``id()`` for the process
+    lifetime: the same layer object always maps to the same slot with no
+    round-robin across forwards or replays. Only integer ids are retained, so
+    the pool never keeps layer objects alive. Distinct layers are assigned
